Element is just a generic term we use to describe anything that we can use on the webpage.
Syntax are rules on how coding language should be written.
attribute name tells us what we are modifying and the attrubute value tells us what we are modifying it to.
target attribute determines whether the attribute value opens in the current page in regards to anchor tag attribute. if no target is set i.e <a href="https://www.youtube.com/"> Link to youtube</a> it will open in the current page. and if target is set to _blank the link element will open in a new tab.
href attribute modifies where the link goes and the target attribute modifies whether this link opens in a new tab or in the current page. and they only work on the link element.
CSS Selector e.g  button {}
CSS Property e.g  backgroung-color: red;
CSS Value e.g red
px - pixels
class attribute - lets us label html elements. to target the class attribute in css we start with a dot then the class name.
in CSS space is called margin.
trick to getting round buttons you have to set the border radius to half the height or width, whichever is lowest.




CSS Box Model: Margin spacing on the outside of an element(e.g button). Can be added on all 4 directions i.e top right bottom left. Padding spancing on the inside of an element(e.g button) also set on all 4 directions. Border is the space between the margin and padding.

CSS Box Model determines how much space an element takes up on the page and how far it is away from other elements. Example:    padding: 10px 16px 10px 16px; (good thing about padding is if text is longer it wont overflow but will fit in the viewport hence a button resizes with text as compared to height and width which does not). 

paragraph tag <p> by default, come with margin at the top and bottom.

The selector that is more specific is going to have a higher priority.

span text element lets us modify a specific part of the text without affecting the whole thing and is the most flexible making it possible to style it in any way we want.